@crew park-noor
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hi. Park, night Watch. I'll show you the patrol route if you're ever up late.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hi, {me}. Picked up an extra shift. That's another plank of the boat.
- Hello, {me}. Locker tidy? Mine is. I've labelled the labels.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Oh, hi, {me}. I'm glad you came by. It's been a long week.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good patrol. Quiet decks. I worked out the boat's sail, in my head.
? mood:low
- Tired. Two shifts back to back. The boat had better be worth it.
== near
? act:leisure
- I'm learning the guitar, badly. There's a waiting list for the book.   #funny
? habit:stargazer
- I pick out the stars over Coriel. You can't see them from here. I pretend.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I'm saving for a boat on Coriel. A small one. Blue, I think.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- The boat. Water slapping the side, nothing to fix, nowhere to be. One day.
